## Interface: 20506
## Category: Commander
## Title: Commander Tracer
## Author: Devin
## Version: 1.0.0
## Notes: Floating combat text, rebuilt as tracer fire: see where every shot lands. Six lanes, each its own anchored, draggable frame with its own motion (scroll, fountain, pop, or a sliding stack), face, size, outline, colour rule and merge window -- your damage, your healing, what lands on you, what heals you, a LEDGER column that holds each event long enough to be read after the fact the way a strategy game reports a finished building (icon, text, tinted accent, repeats merged into one row with a count), and big CALLOUTS for the moments: a killing blow, an interrupt you landed, a dispel, a proc lighting up. Fed by the combat log rather than Blizzard's text events, so every number carries its spell, its icon, its school and its target, and misses arrive as the word for what went wrong. Twenty-two kinds of event, each routed to any lane or none and optionally to the ledger; numbers plain, separated or short; crits marked, sized and punched; partials in brackets on request; four sounds. Blizzard's own text -- the engine's numbers over units and the scrolling text round your character -- is switched off while this runs and handed back exactly when it stops. The rules run under plain luajit with no client attached.
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\Ability_Marksmanship
## SavedVariables: CommanderTracerDB
## RequiredDeps: Commander_Events
## OptionalDeps: Commander_Console

